<div class="cp-grid cp-grid-2">
  <div class="cp-card">
    <h3 class="cp-card-title">Getting started</h3>
    <ol class="cp-secondary" style="padding-left:1.1rem; line-height:1.9; font-size:0.875rem">
      <li><strong>Register your website</strong> &mdash; the domain you enter is the only domain your Site API Key will work on.</li>
      <li><strong>Connect an AI provider</strong> &mdash; paste your own OpenAI or Gemini key. It is encrypted and never leaves our servers.</li>
      <li><strong>Test the connection</strong> &mdash; Chat Pilot discovers the models your key can actually use.</li>
      <li><strong>Build your Knowledge Base</strong> &mdash; scan your site, add FAQs, paste manual facts, upload documents.</li>
      <li><strong>Tune AI Instructions</strong> &mdash; tone, length, and what to say when it does not know.</li>
      <li><strong>Try the Developer Chat Preview</strong> &mdash; same engine as the live widget, with diagnostics.</li>
      <li><strong>Generate a Site API Key</strong> and paste it into the WordPress plugin.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="cp-card">
    <h3 class="cp-card-title">Troubleshooting</h3>
    <dl class="cp-secondary" style="font-size:0.875rem; line-height:1.7">
      <dt><strong>&ldquo;Domain Mismatch&rdquo; in WordPress</strong></dt>
      <dd style="margin:0 0 0.9rem">The site URL does not match the registered domain. Update the Website URL on the Connection tab, or add the hostname as an additional allowed domain.</dd>

      <dt><strong>The bot always says it cannot find information</strong></dt>
      <dd style="margin:0 0 0.9rem">Your Knowledge Base is empty or the retrieval threshold is too high. Use Retrieval Diagnostics on the Knowledge Base tab to see actual scores.</dd>

      <dt><strong>&ldquo;Having trouble generating a response&rdquo;</strong></dt>
      <dd style="margin:0 0 0.9rem">That is the AI provider failure message, not a knowledge problem. Check AI Providers &rarr; connection status; usually a quota or an expired key.</dd>

      <dt><strong>Widget does not appear</strong></dt>
      <dd style="margin:0 0 0.9rem">Check that the widget is enabled on the Chat Widget tab, the website status is Active, and the plugin shows Connected.</dd>

      <dt><strong>Models list is empty</strong></dt>
      <dd style="margin:0">Run &ldquo;Test connection &amp; discover models&rdquo;. Chat Pilot never shows a hardcoded model list &mdash; if your key cannot use a model, it will not appear.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</div>

